        <headline>High Wind Warning issued September 25 at 8:03AM PDT until September 25 at 11:00AM PDT by NWS Portland OR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...West winds 30 to 40 mph with gusts up to 70 mph.

* WHERE...In Oregon, Clatsop County Coast. In Washington, Pacific
County Coast.

* WHEN...Until 11 AM PDT this morning.

* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will produce widely scattered tree damage
and power outages. Travel will be difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The strongest winds will be along beaches and
headlands. Coastal communities will generally see gusts up to 50 to
60 mph.
</description>
        <instruction>People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around
or damaged by the wind.

Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.</instruction>
